Sentence pronunciation policy:
- Explicit reviewed example Pinyin is authoritative, including polyphones,
  citation tones, unmarked neutral tones, ü, apostrophes and attached erhua r.
- Hanzi/Pinyin punctuation and clause boundaries must align. Chinese and ASCII
  commas, periods, questions, exclamations, semicolons and colons normalize to
  model punctuation; enumeration comma becomes a comma. No punctuation is
  discarded and no tone sandhi crosses a punctuation boundary.
- Each Hanzi clause reuses scripts/generate-audio.py unchanged for base phonetic
  conversion and contextual sandhi, with the grammar-only yi correction below.
  Punctuation is restored in the full sentence phoneme sequence for pauses and
  question intonation.
- Citation yi1 remains unchanged at numeral/ordinal positions, in decimals and
  at the end of multi-syllable Pinyin words such as shiyi, zhouyi and tongyi.
  Other yi1 takes contextual sandhi. Before a neutral syllable, only its
  underlying tone is consulted among readings matching the explicit Pinyin
  base (e.g. ge5 has underlying ge4); the authored neutral tone is retained.
- Unknown model phonemes, misalignment and more than 510 phoneme tokens abort
  generation; there is no inferred-reading fallback, splitting or truncation.
- Deterministic jieba phrasing approximates contextual third-tone grouping;
  no human auditory validation of synthesized sentences is claimed.

Encoding: MP3, libmp3lame 64kbps, 24000Hz, mono. Every new MP3 is fully decoded
and checked for finite samples, meaningful duration and non-silent RMS.
Identical final sentence phonemes may reuse a synthesis, copied to each
example ID. Files are named G<level>-<rule ordinal>-<example ordinal>.mp3.
manifest.json records full source text/Pinyin, individual clauses and their
citation/surface readings, full punctuation-bearing phonemes, audio SHA256,
duration, RMS, bytes, both generator hashes, model/settings/dependency hashes
and input file hashes. Resume only trusts matching fingerprints and checksums.
The grammar corpus does not alter or regenerate the existing vocabulary audio.
